" href=\"/icon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri+Quran&family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Naskh+Arabic:wght@400;600&display=swap\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/theme.css\">\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);padding:20px 16px 48px;line-height:1.6}.tr{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}.cr{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.ar{direction:rtl;text-align:right}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"sp\"><nav class=\"crumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> › <a href=\"/en/surah/15.html\">Surah Al-Hijr</a> › Verse 91</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah Al-Hijr 15:91</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿الَّذِينَ جَعَلُوا الْقُرْآنَ عِضِينَ﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">Who have made the Qur’ān into portions.</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">أي: قسموه فآمنوا ببعضه وكفروا ببعضه<cite>«بيان تلبيس الجهمية في تأسيس بدعهم الكلامية» 1/259</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s15a91\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><a href=\"/en/ayah/15-75.html\">Previous verse (15:75)</a><a href=\"/en/ayah/15-92.html\">Next verse (15:92)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n","ayah/15-92.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tafsir of Al-Hijr 15:92 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"So by your Lord, We will surely question them all\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ar\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"x-default\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"en\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ur\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ur/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"id\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/id/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"tr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/tr/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fr/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"bn\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/bn/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ms\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ms/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fa\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fa/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ru\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ru/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"sw\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/sw/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ha\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ha/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"es\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/es/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"de\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/de/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"zh\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/zh/ayah/15-92.html\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Tafsir of Al-Hijr 15:92 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"So by your Lord, We will surely question them all\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1f4d3a\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/og.png\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Surah Al-Hijr\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/surah/15.html\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Verse 92\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-92.html\"}]}</script>\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/icon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri+Quran&family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Naskh+Arabic:wght@400;600&display=swap\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/theme.css\">\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);padding:20px 16px 48px;line-height:1.6}.tr{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}.cr{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.ar{direction:rtl;text-align:right}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"sp\"><nav class=\"crumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> › <a href=\"/en/surah/15.html\">Surah Al-Hijr</a> › Verse 92</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah Al-Hijr 15:92</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿فَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَسْأَلَنَّهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">So by your Lord, We will surely question them all</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">وإما على جملة طلبية كقوله تعالى: {فوربك لنسألنهم أجمعين} {عما كانوا يعملون} مع أن هذا القسم قد يراد به تحقيق المقسم عليه فيكون من باب الخبر وقد يراد به محض القسم.<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 13/315</cite></blockquote><h3>What he quoted from others</h3><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\"><span class=\"who\">أبو العالية</span> <span class=\"st\">أقرّه</span> «خلتان تسأل العباد يوم القيامة عنهما: عما كانوا يعملون وعما أجابوا الرسل.»<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 27/274</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s15a92\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><a href=\"/en/ayah/15-91.html\">Previous verse (15:91)</a><a href=\"/en/ayah/15-93.html\">Next verse (15:93)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n","ayah/15-93.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tafsir of Al-Hijr 15:93 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"About what they used to do.\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ar\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"x-default\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"en\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ur\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ur/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"id\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/id/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"tr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/tr/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fr/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"bn\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/bn/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ms\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ms/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fa\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fa/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ru\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ru/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"sw\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/sw/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ha\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ha/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"es\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/es/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"de\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/de/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"zh\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/zh/ayah/15-93.html\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Tafsir of Al-Hijr 15:93 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"About what they used to do.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1f4d3a\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/og.png\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Surah Al-Hijr\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/surah/15.html\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Verse 93\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-93.html\"}]}</script>\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/icon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri+Quran&family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Naskh+Arabic:wght@400;600&display=swap\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/theme.css\">\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);padding:20px 16px 48px;line-height:1.6}.tr{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}.cr{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.ar{direction:rtl;text-align:right}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"sp\"><nav class=\"crumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> › <a href=\"/en/surah/15.html\">Surah Al-Hijr</a> › Verse 93</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah Al-Hijr 15:93</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿عَمَّا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">About what they used to do.</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">فالأولى تحقيق شهادة أن لا إله إلا الله والثانية تحقيق الشهادة بأن محمدا رسول<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 19/172</cite></blockquote><h3>What he quoted from others</h3><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\"><span class=\"who\">أبو العالية</span> <span class=\"st\">أقرّه</span> «خلتان يسأل عنهما كل أحد: ماذا كنت تعبد؟ وماذا أجبت المرسلين؟»<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 19/172</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s15a93\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><a href=\"/en/ayah/15-92.html\">Previous verse (15:92)</a><a href=\"/en/ayah/15-99.html\">Next verse (15:99)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n","ayah/15-99.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tafsir of Al-Hijr 15:99 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"And worship your Lord until there comes to you the certainty [i.e., death].\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ar\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"x-default\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"en\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ur\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ur/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"id\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/id/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"tr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/tr/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fr/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"bn\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/bn/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ms\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ms/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fa\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fa/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ru\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ru/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"sw\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/sw/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ha\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ha/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"es\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/es/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"de\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/de/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"zh\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/zh/ayah/15-99.html\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Tafsir of Al-Hijr 15:99 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"And worship your Lord until there comes to you the certainty [i.e., death].\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1f4d3a\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/og.png\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Surah Al-Hijr\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/surah/15.html\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Verse 99\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/15-99.html\"}]}</script>\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/icon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri+Quran&family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Naskh+Arabic:wght@400;600&display=swap\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/theme.css\">\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);padding:20px 16px 48px;line-height:1.6}.tr{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}.cr{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.ar{direction:rtl;text-align:right}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"sp\"><nav class=\"crumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> › <a href=\"/en/surah/15.html\">Surah Al-Hijr</a> › Verse 99</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah Al-Hijr 15:99</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿وَاعْبُدْ رَبَّكَ حَتَّىٰ يَأْتِيَكَ الْيَقِينُ﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">And worship your Lord until there comes to you the certainty [i.e., death].</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">وهذا خطأ بإجماع المسلمين أهل التفسير وغيرهم فإن المسلمين متفقون على أن وجوب العبادات كالصلوات الخمس ونحوها وتحريم المرحمات كالفواحش والمظالم لا يزال واجبا على كل أحد ما دام عقله حاضرا، ولو بلغ، وأن الصلوات لا تسقط عن أحد قط إلا عن الحائض والنفساء أو من زال عقله.<cite>«درء تعارض العقل والنقل» 3/270</cite></blockquote><h3>What he quoted from others</h3><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\"><span class=\"who\">بعض المنتسبين إلى التصوف</span> <span class=\"st\">ردّه</span> «ويقول معناها: اعبد ربك حتى يحصل لك العلم والمعرفة فإذا حصل ذلك سقطت العبادة.»<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 11/417</cite></blockquote></section><section><h2>Imam Ibn al-Qayyim</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">واليقين هاهنا هو الموت بإجماع أهل التفسير<cite>«مدارج السالكين بين منازل إياك نعبد وإياك نستعين» 1/124</cite></blockquote><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">فلا ينفك العبد من العبودية ما دام في دار التكليف<cite>«مدارج السالكين بين منازل إياك نعبد وإياك نستعين» 1/124</cite></blockquote><h3>What he quoted from others</h3><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\"><span class=\"who\">بعض أهل الشطح (اليقين: شهود الحقيقة)</span> <span class=\"st\">ردّه</span> «من شهد الحقيقة سقط عنه الأمر، ويحتجون بقوله تعالى {واعبد ربك حتى يأتيك اليقين} [الحجر: 99] ويفسرون اليقين بشهود الحكم الكوني»<cite>«مدارج السالكين بين منازل إياك نعبد وإياك نستعين» 1/182</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s15a99\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><a href=\"/en/ayah/15-93.html\">Previous verse (15:93)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\">